# ===================================================================
# HyperVerse Environment Variables
# ===================================================================
# Copy to `.env` for local overrides. `.env` is gitignored — never commit it.
#
# This app makes no network requests. Every variable below is OPTIONAL and
# affects only developer tooling; none of them are read by application code at
# runtime, with the single exception of EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN noted below.
#
# The app previously shipped placeholder entries for a hosted OpenAI key,
# Ethereum/Polygon RPC endpoints, analytics, and SSL certificate pinning. None
# were ever read by any module, and a template that invites a developer to paste
# a real API key into a file the app ignores is a liability. They are gone.
# ===================================================================

# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Replit deployment (only for the Replit workflow)
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by the `dev:replit` script. Leave unset when running locally.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DOMAIN=your-repl-domain.replit.app
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REPL_ID=your-repl-id

# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Crash reporting
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE VARIABLE THAT CHANGES DATA FLOW. When set, `lib/logger.ts`
# initialises sentry-expo and log payloads (already redacted by
# `redact()` in that file) are sent to Sentry from release builds only.
#
# Leaving this unset means no data leaves the device. If you set it, say so in
# the release notes — it is the only way this app transmits anything.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0

# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Developer tooling
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verbose Metro output while developing.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEBUG_MODE=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On-device AI models
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No model files are bundled. The assistant answers from a local engine over your
# own records by default, and only runs a downloaded language model if one has
# been fetched to the app sandbox. See lib/ai/models/ModelManager.ts.
